{title: SUMMER IN THE ATTIC}
{key: C}
{capo: 2}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Boxes full of p[F]hotographs
[C]Fading at the co[G]rners now
[C]Every one a litt[F]le laugh
[Am]I forget the [G]words somehow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_prechorus: Pre-Chorus}
[F]And the dust i[G]s dancing
[F]In the only be[G]am of light
{end_of_prechorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus (x2)}
[C]Summer in t[G]he attic, [Am]summer [F]in my head
[C]Every song [G]we used to s[F]ing, [C]every word we said
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Grandpa's coat i[F]s on a hook
[C]Smelling still [G]of pipe and rain
[C]Pages of a cooker[F]y book
[Am]Wrote her name [G]and wrote it again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_prechorus: Pre-Chorus}
[F]And the dust i[G]s dancing
[F]In the only be[G]am of light
{end_of_prechorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus (x2)}
[C]Summer in t[G]he attic, [Am]summer [F]in my head
[C]Every song [G]we used to s[F]ing, [C]every word we said
{end_of_chorus}
